# Git commits: no Cursor author

Commits in this repo belong to the existing local Git identity (`user.name` / `user.email`). Do not change `git config`.

When creating a commit:

- Do **not** set `--author` to Cursor or any AI name
- Do **not** set `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL`, `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL` to Cursor
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: claude`, or any AI trailer
- Do **not** put Cursor in the commit message body or sign-off

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git commit --author="Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>" -m "..."
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat: add desk

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
EOF
)"

# ✅ GOOD — default local user only
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat: add desk mint/redeem flow

EOF
)"
```

If a hook injects a Cursor trailer, amend only when the commit is still local, created in this session, and unpushed; otherwise make a follow-up commit that does not repeat the trailer.
